### : :II:
### : Test that depexts only works correctly and only install depexts of new packages
### <pkg:to-update.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-update-1"]
### <pkg:to-update.2>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-update-2"]
### <pkg:to-remove.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-remove"]
### <pkg:to-install.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-install"]
depends: ["to-install-dep" "already-installed-dep"]
conflicts: ["to-remove"]
### <pkg:to-install-dep.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-install-dep"]
### <pkg:already-installed-dep.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-already-installed-dep"]
### <pkg:to-reinstall.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-reinstall-1"]
### opam update default

<><> Updating package repositories ><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
[default] synchronised from file://${BASEDIR}/REPO
Now run 'opam upgrade' to apply any package updates.
### opam switch create --empty depexts-only
### OPAMYES=1
### opam-set-os dummy-success
Added '[os-family "dummy-success" "Set through 'opam var'"]' to field global-variables in global configuration
### : :II:1 here we first install to-update.1, to-remove.1, to-reinstall.1 and
### : already-installed-dep.1, voluntarily passing --no-depexts so their
### : respective depexts are not installed but the packages are.
### opam install to-update.1 to-remove.1 to-reinstall.1 already-installed-dep.1 --no-depexts
The following actions will be performed:
=== install 4 packages
  - install already-installed-dep 1
  - install to-reinstall          1
  - install to-remove             1
  - install to-update             1

<><> Processing actions <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
-> installed already-installed-dep.1
-> installed to-reinstall.1
-> installed to-remove.1
-> installed to-update.1
Done.
### <pkg:to-reinstall.1>
opam-version: "2.0"
depexts: ["ext-to-reinstall-2"]
### opam update default

<><> Updating package repositories ><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>
[default] synchronised from file://${BASEDIR}/REPO
### opam reinstall --list-pending
[WARNING] Opam packages already-installed-dep.1, to-reinstall.1, to-remove.1 and to-update.1 depend on the following system packages that are no longer installed: ext-already-installed-dep ext-to-reinstall-2 ext-to-remove ext-to-update-1
to-reinstall.1
to-remove.1
to-update.1
already-installed-dep.1
### : :II:2 We then try to install to-update.2 and to-install.1 with --depext-only.
### : The solution will contain the removal of to-remove.1 because of the conflict with c.1
### : and to-update.1 will be upgraded to to-update.2.
### : Since we modified the metadata of to-reinstall.1, it should be listed for reinstall.
### : The command should only install depexts for new packages in the solution, i.e.
### : depexts of to-update.2, to-install.1, to-install-dep.1 and already-installed-dep.1
### : which is already installed but in the solution dependency cone and needs its
### : depexts installed.
### opam install to-update.2 to-install.1 --depext-only | sed-cmd echo
[WARNING] Opam packages already-installed-dep.1, to-reinstall.1, to-remove.1 and to-update.1 depend on the following system packages that are no longer installed: ext-already-installed-dep ext-to-reinstall-2 ext-to-remove ext-to-update-1

The following system packages will first need to be installed:
    ext-already-installed-dep ext-to-install ext-to-install-dep ext-to-update-2

<><> Handling external dependencies <><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><><>

+ echo "ext-already-installed-dep" "ext-to-install" "ext-to-install-dep" "ext-to-update-2"
- ext-already-installed-dep ext-to-install ext-to-install-dep ext-to-update-2
